&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:86px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:86px;left:119px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft13"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:83px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;Постановление Президента Республики Узбекистан «О мерах по поднятию на качественно &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:102px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft19"&gt;новый  уровень  деятельности  по  популяризации  изучения  иностранных  языков  в  Республике &lt;br/&gt;Узбекистан». ПП-5117 от 19 – мая 2021 года. &lt;br/&gt;2.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:143px;left:119px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft13"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:140px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;Редько  Л.Л.,  Леонова  Н.А.  Антропологическая  парадигма  профессиональной  подготовки &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:159px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft19"&gt;педагогов  в  системе  вузовского  образования:  методологический  аспект  //  Фундаментальные &lt;br/&gt;исследования. 2015, №. – С. 2-15. URL: http://www.fundamental-research.ru/ru/article/view?id=37792 &lt;br/&gt;(дата обращения: 03.01.2021). &lt;br/&gt;3.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:219px;left:119px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft13"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:219px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Berta_Barquero"&gt;Barquero  &lt;/a&gt;B.,  Bosch  M.  Didactic  Engineering  as  a  Research  Methodology:  From  Fundamental &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:238px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft110"&gt;Situations  to  Study  and  Research  Paths.  //  In  book:  New  ICMI  Study  Series:  Task  Design  in &lt;br/&gt;Mathematics  Education.  /A.  Watson,  M.  Ohtani  Eds.  –  Springer  International  Publishing  Switzerland, &lt;br/&gt;2015. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:273px;left:186px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;– &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:276px;left:236px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;P.249-272. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:276px;left:351px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.researchgate.net/publication/283572351_Didactic_Engineering%20_as_a_Research_Methodology_From_Fundamental_Situations_to_Study_and_Research_Paths"&gt;www.researchgate.net/publication/283572351_Didactic_Engineering &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:295px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft110"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.researchgate.net/publication/283572351_Didactic_Engineering%20_as_a_Research_Methodology_From_Fundamental_Situations_to_Study_and_Research_Paths"&gt;_as_a_Research_Methodology_From_Fundamental_Situations_to_Study_and_Research_Paths. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;DOI:&lt;a href="https://www.researchgate.net/deref/http%3A%2F%2Fdx.doi.org%2F10.1007%2F978-3-319-09629-2_8"&gt; 10.1007/978-3-319-09629-2_8 &lt;br/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:332px;left:119px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft13"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:333px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;Tchoshanov M. Engineering of Learning: Conceptualizing e-Didactics.  – UNESCO  Institute for &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:352px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft110"&gt;Information Technologies in Education, 2013. &lt;br/&gt;5.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:371px;left:119px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft13"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:371px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft14"&gt;&lt;a href="https://evolkov.net/moodle/mod/forum/discuss.php?d=2150"&gt;https://evolkov.net/moodle/mod/forum/discuss.php?d=2150&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:371px;left:555px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;&lt;a href="https://evolkov.net/moodle/mod/forum/discuss.php?d=2150"&gt; &lt;/a&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:390px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft110"&gt; &lt;br/&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:428px;left:112px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft11"&gt;&lt;b&gt;FOREIGN LANGUAGE PROFICIENCY CERTIFICATE AS A COMPETITIVE ADVANTAGE &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:447px;left:358px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft11"&gt;&lt;b&gt;IN THE LABOR MARKET &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:466px;left:678px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft15"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Babaniyazova N.P.  &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:485px;left:321px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft16"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Doctor of philosophy (PhD) on pedagogical sciences, associate professor  &lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:504px;left:496px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft16"&gt;&lt;i&gt; NSPI named after Ajiniyaz, Nukus, Uzbekistan  &lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:523px;left:568px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft16"&gt;&lt;i&gt;e-mail:&lt;a href="mailto:babaniyazova1983@mail.ru"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:523px;left:620px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft17"&gt;&lt;a href="mailto:babaniyazova1983@mail.ru"&gt;&lt;i&gt;babaniyazova1983@mail.ru&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:523px;left:808px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft16"&gt;&lt;a href="mailto:babaniyazova1983@mail.ru"&gt;&lt;i&gt; &lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;i&gt; &lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:542px;left:170px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:561px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;Certificate  is  a  document  confirming  knowledge  of  a  foreign  language  and  recognized  by &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:580px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft110"&gt;educational  institutions,  employers  and  other  organizations  in  different  countries  of  the  world.  The &lt;br/&gt;certificate can be obtained passing special exams in a foreign language, which developed and maintained &lt;br/&gt;by both private and public organizations. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:637px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;Today, teachers of New Uzbekistan are increasingly working on themselves, studying and testing &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:656px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft110"&gt;their knowledge of a foreign language. Progress in learning a foreign language begins with the adoption &lt;br/&gt;of  the  Decree  of  the  President  of  the  Republic  of  Uzbekistan  dated  May  19,  2021  No.  PP-5117  ―On &lt;br/&gt;measures to raise to a qualitatively new level activities to promote the study of foreign languages  in the &lt;br/&gt;Republic  of  Uzbekistan‖,  where  teachers  of  foreign  languages  of  general  secondary,  secondary &lt;br/&gt;specialized  and  professional  educational  institutions  that  have  a  national  or  corresponding  international &lt;br/&gt;certificate of a level not lower than C1, are exempted from testing in a foreign language module with an &lt;br/&gt;assessment of the maximum score for qualification tests during the test. At the same time, obtaining this &lt;br/&gt;certificate  is  recognized  as  an  alternative  form  of  advanced training.  Also,  starting  from  the  2021-2022 &lt;br/&gt;academic year, foreign language teachers of educational institutions who have a national or corresponding &lt;br/&gt;international certificate of at least C1 level are paid an additional monthly allowance of 50 percent to their &lt;br/&gt;basic tariff rate [1].  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:865px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft110"&gt;What types of certificates are recognized in our republic? &lt;br/&gt;In accordance with the Resolution of the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan No. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:903px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft18"&gt;312  dated  May  19,  2021  &amp;#34;On  measures  to  effectively  organize  the  promotion  of  the  study  of  foreign &lt;br/&gt;languages&amp;#34;,  international  certificates  such  as  International  English  Language  Testing  System  (IELTS), &lt;br/&gt;Test  of  English as  a  Foreign  Language  (TOEFL  iBT),  Test  of  English  as  a  Foreign  Language  (TOEFL &lt;br/&gt;ITP),  Cambridge  Assessment  English,  APTIS  for  teachers,  Test  of  English  for  International &lt;br/&gt;Communication (TOEIC), Lingua skill, Teaching Knowledge Test (TKT), Teaching English for Speakers &lt;br/&gt;of Other Languages (TESOL), Teaching English as a Foreign Language (TEFL), Teaching English as a &lt;br/&gt;Second  Language  (TESL),  Certificate  in  English  Language  Teaching  to  Adults  (CELTA),  Diploma  in &lt;br/&gt;Teaching  English  to  Speakers  of  Other  Languages  (DELTA)  recognized  in  the  Republic  of  Uzbekistan &lt;br/&gt;[2]. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1073px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;Now,  you  are  thinking  about  getting  an  international  certificate.  So  how  do  you  know  which &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1092px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;exam you really need? First of all, you need to answer the following questions:  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1111px;left:160px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft12"&gt;1. In which country are you going to use the certificate? With English, the situation is as follows: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1130px;left:106px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft110"&gt;taking TOEFL - an American English test - is often pointless if you are going to Europe, but almost all &lt;br/&gt;US  universities  require  this  particular  certificate;  Canada,  despite  its  proximity  to  the  United  States, &lt;br/&gt;accepts the IELTS certificate.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;







 &lt;br/&gt;
&lt;style type="text/css"&gt;
&lt;!--
	p {margin: 0; padding: 0;}	.ft20{font-size:16px;font-family:Calibri;color:#000000;}
	.ft21{font-size:16px;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;}
	.ft22{font-size:16px;font-family:Times New Roman,Bold;color:#000000;}
	.ft23{font-size:16px;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;}
	.ft24{font-size:16px;line-height:18px;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;}
	.ft25{font-size:16px;line-height:19px;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;}
	.ft26{font-size:16px;line-height:15px;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;}
	.ft27{font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;}
--&gt;
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;div class="sub_page"&gt;
&lt;div id="page2-div" style="position:relative;width:892px;height:1262px;"&gt;
&lt;img width="892" height="1262" src="/files/journals/46/articles/5548/628f36283c8c7002.jpg" alt="background image"/&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1203px;left:423px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft20"&gt;159 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:68px;left:138px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft21"&gt;2. Why do you need an international certificate? As a rule, we set the following goals: - getting a &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:86px;left:85px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft25"&gt;job; - getting an education; - emigration and citizenship; - own ambitions or desire to confirm the level of &lt;br/&gt;foreign  language  proficiency  by  an  independent  commission.  Do  you  want  to  study  at  a  foreign &lt;br/&gt;university? Get ready for a serious IELTS test, and, preferably, for a very decent score, at least 7.5. For &lt;br/&gt;admission to an educational institution in the United States, TOEFL is required, and the score must also &lt;br/&gt;be  high  enough.  At  the  same  time,  it  should  be  borne  in  mind  that  after  two  years  these  certificates &lt;br/&gt;become invalid, so there is no need to take these exams without deciding on the date of departure. 3. At &lt;br/&gt;what level do you speak a foreign language at this stage and how much time do you have to prepare for &lt;br/&gt;the chosen exam? Before setting a goal to get this or that international certificate, think about whether you &lt;br/&gt;have enough time to prepare for it and the knowledge to pass it successfully. Some exams require serious &lt;br/&gt;and regular study for months and sometimes years. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:276px;left:138px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft21"&gt;In March 2022, at the Nukus State Pedagogical Institute, teachers of the interfaculty department &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:295px;left:85px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft25"&gt;of  foreign  languages  conducted  an  analysis  among  students  of  six  departments.  The  goal  is  the  needs &lt;br/&gt;analysis  of  ESP  students  was  to  provide  faculty  with  information  to  ―make  informed  decisions―  about &lt;br/&gt;planning designing and delivering English instruction in each major area, as per the collective voice of the &lt;br/&gt;students. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:371px;left:138px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft21"&gt;Participants worked in cluster teams and prepared and applied their surveys to students, reported &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:390px;left:85px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft26"&gt;their  findings,  and  reflected  on  their  plans  for  future  syllabus  designs  that  would  satisfy  the  needs  and &lt;br/&gt;desires of their students, and highlight the current importance of English on the global stage. Matrix of &lt;br/&gt;findings across six departments exploring student voices: student perspectives of ESP at NSPI in picture &lt;br/&gt;№1. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:886px;left:784px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft21"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:901px;left:138px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft21"&gt;In total, student voices were heard by way of six department surveys and data suggests that most &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:920px;left:85px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft24"&gt;students want to learn English to successfully navigate the different English standardized tests, which will &lt;br/&gt;allow them to attend graduate school in both Uzbekistan, and abroad. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:958px;left:138px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft21"&gt;They also indicated a strong desire and motivation to improve their spoken and listening skills, to &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:977px;left:85px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft25"&gt;be prepared in English to follow their dreams and be successful in their professional and personal lives. &lt;br/&gt;Accordingly, a national or corresponding international certificate of the level of knowledge of a foreign &lt;br/&gt;language is the highest need in educational institutions of our republic. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1034px;left:462px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft22"&gt;&lt;b&gt; &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1053px;left:404px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft22"&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES: &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1072px;left:85px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft21"&gt;1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1071px;left:97px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft23"&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1072px;left:138px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft21"&gt;Resolution of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated May 19, 2021 No. PP-5117 &amp;#34;On &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="position:absolute;top:1091px;left:85px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft25"&gt;measures to raise to a qualitatively new level of activities to popularize the study of foreign languages in &lt;br/&gt;the Republic of Uzbekistan&amp;#34;. &lt;br/&gt;2. Resolution of the Cabinet of Ministers of the Republic of Uzbekistan No. 312 dated May 19, 2021 &amp;#34;On &lt;br/&gt;measures for the effective organization of the popularization of foreign language learning&amp;#34;. &lt;br/&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

